From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Roles & Permissions: rail+detail redesign, staged saves

Rewrites ProtonRolesPermissionsPage.vue (created by 0027, extended by 0028's
Chatwoot-access section, root div touched by 0051) and adds a small
protonChatwootAgents.js API helper.

What changes, and why:

* Layout. A `<select>` that hid every role behind a click becomes a role rail
  showing each role's id, description, permission count and member count at a
  glance. The always-open "New role id / Name / Create role" form that sat
  between the picker and the permission list becomes an inline composer that
  only opens on demand, with the id auto-slugged from the name.

* Staged saves. Every control used to fire its own grant/revoke immediately
  and then re-fetch, so a mis-click was already committed and there was no
  feedback either way. Everything now mutates a local draft and a save bar
  reports the diff. Save replays the diff one call per change, in order,
  stopping at the first failure -- then re-reads the server and re-stages
  exactly what never ran, so a partial save says so instead of silently
  half-applying. Sequential, not concurrent: native-key writes resync the
  Chatwoot role mirror for every member of the role, so parallel calls race.

* Permissions are grouped, searchable and counted, and the row now leads with
  the human sentence ("Trigger KB document ingestion") over the dotted key in
  mono beneath it, rather than "kb.ingest -- Trigger KB document ingestion".
  Grouping is presentation only: any key the backend returns that this file
  does not know about falls into an "Other" group. That matters in practice --
  the live proton tenant's backend returns 12 keys while seed.py in this
  checkout defines 20 -- and a permission that exists but cannot be seen is a
  permission that cannot be administered.

* Members. The list rendered bare numeric Chatwoot user ids ("1", "6") and
  membership was edited by typing an id into a text box. It now resolves ids
  against Chatwoot's own /api/v1/accounts/:id/agents (name, email, avatar) and
  assigns from a searchable picker. The directory call is fail-open: if it
  returns nothing the page falls back to the raw-id entry it had before, so
  membership stays editable regardless. Ids with no matching agent render as
  "User #N -- not found in this account" rather than disappearing.

* Self-lockout guard. Revoking `roles.manage` from your own role, or removing
  yourself from the only role granting it, made this page unreachable with no
  in-product way back. `wouldLoseAccess` evaluates that across all roles with
  the draft overlaid, and routes Save through an explicit confirmation.

* "Default access" is a new first option in the conversation-visibility radio
  group, meaning "none of the three native keys granted". The previous UI had
  no way back to that state once a radio had been picked, even though it is
  the state every role ships in (seed.py auto-grants native keys to no role).

Unsaved changes are guarded on both role switch and route leave via an
in-app prompt. No backend change: this uses only the /authz endpoints that
already exist, so it ships with a Chatwoot image rebuild alone.

NOTE: the pre-image for ProtonRolesPermissionsPage.vue was reconstructed by
replaying 0027 -> 0028 -> 0051 with `git apply` into a scratch repo (all three
applied clean), and this patch was then verified to apply on top of that same
replay. This sandbox still has no network access to clone upstream, so the
patch has NOT been checked against a real fork checkout -- but unlike the
hand-constructed patches in this directory, its context lines are machine-
generated from a byte-exact pre-image rather than transcribed. Verify with
`git apply --check` or a full image build before staging.
